plugin-hostd (0.20.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * clients: the short forms of plan, plan_get and estimate are errors, as
    protocol 0.7.0 made their trailing fields mandatory
  * docs/guide.md: regenerated against plugin-hostd-protocol 0.7.0
  * release 0.20.8: floors at plugin-hostd-protocol 0.7.0 and omx-clap-core
    0.33.1
  * release 0.20.8: the changelog entry names what main added since the
    branch point
  * packaging: build-depend on sqlite's development files, which the Debian
    reader package does not pull in
  * ci: the rpm job's artifact no longer shares the release build's name
  * ci: the deb smoke compares the daemon version with the package's upstream
    version
  * ci: the deb smoke container adds the OpenMixer channel instead of a
    hand-kept download list
  * ci: the deb smoke installs every channel dependency the floors name
  * proc: proc_term of a worker already stopped adds no second entry
  * proc_term test: a worker stopped twice leaves one entry, none once reaped
  * clients/ts: omx-contract is a floor only
  * deps: the lockfile resolves @openmixer/omx-contract 3.20.2
  * tests: the packaged daemon is checked to carry no test seam for the
    qualification store
  * ci: the deb jobs take their cells from check-matrix and run on the ARM
    runner
  * proc: the stopped-worker list grows instead of dropping past 64 (#153)
  * clients/ts: the codec command decides "run, not imported" with isMain
  * clients/ts: test the codec command through a symlinked bin (red)
  * ci: the contract rpm's expected file list holds the machine and probe
    domains
  * qualification store: no protocol conf key, the test seam is a test-build
    variable; queries start from PQDB_QUERY_ANY
  * tests/consumer: a ledger of replace-keyed is a known kind of the protocol
    0.6 header
  * tests: the daemon makes no qualification directory
  * tests/contract_derived: the generator test reads plugin-db's domain from
    the installed contract directory too
  * tests: a cell figure given as a number is read as itself
  * qualcost: document the reader's header for the doxygen gate, and export
    PKG_CONFIG_PATH in the temporary CI build
  * ci: build the qualification reader from a pinned commit (temporary, until
    libplugin-qualification-db is published)
  * plugin-hostd reads qualifications through libplugin-qualification-db,
    record files no longer read
  * tests: the daemon tests put the figures in a qualification store, the
    sabotage names the new reader
  * tests: the qualification store fixtures take the installed DDL of
    plugin-qualification-db
  * ci: the rpm arch matrix is a plain list; protocol-gen: a miscounted LISTS
    slot is a build error
  * verbs_ahead: the four property verbs are answered by the daemon, so they
    leave the declared-ahead list
  * tests: plugin-hostd reads qualifications through
    libplugin-qualification-db, red first
  * probe schema: the plugin address formats are read from plugin-db's
    domain, not typed in the template
  * tests/ci_guards: the Fedora 44 scan matches any 44 in a Fedora list
  * ci: Fedora 45 only (F44 dropped), as omx-dsp and omx-clap-core
  * release: 0.20.8
  * packaging: floors at plugin-hostd-protocol 0.6.0 and omx-clap-core
    0.33.0, and no Breaks or Replaces between our packages
  * machine domain: x-since is the domain version that added the item
  * test: an item's x-since is the domain version that added it
  * probe_words.h: document the X macros the enums expand
  * probe domain: the reasons, outcomes, steps and signals a probe run writes
    are a domain the loader opens (green)
  * test: the probe domain: its items are the words the probe writes, and a
    missing one is refused (red)
  * machine domain: MACHINE_FAMILIES, and the probe writes the domain's
    family word (green)
  * tests: arm 8 of the machine domain test: MACHINE_FAMILIES and the probe's
    family from the domain
  * test: one tracked() for the tests that scan the tree
  * tests: arm 2 walks the tree when git answers nothing
  * test: the qualification domain test lists the tree when git refuses the
    checkout
  * Makefile: the format and verbs-alloc tests link the domain loader
  * tests: the added latency method takes the next x-code
  * machine.h: document the band words, the floor and the functions
  * the daemon reads the installed contract directory only; a test build for
    its tests (green)
  * tests: the daemon reads no contract path from the environment (red)
  * the daemon reads the machine domain where OMX_CONTRACT_PATH says (green)
  * tests: the daemon reads the machine domain where OMX_CONTRACT_PATH says
    (red)
  * machine words: read from the machine domain through the loader (green)
  * tests: the machine words are read from the machine domain at start-up
    (red)
  * machine domain: omx-contract fmt --contract-dir contract.d (green)
  * tests: the machine domain is in the one formatting (red)
  * plugin-hostd.spec: the machine domain is
    %{omx_contract_domain_dir}/machine/
  * packaging: plugin-hostd requires plugin-qualify-contract, the data
    package that holds the qualification domain
  * qualification_words.h: every parameter, return and macro is documented
  * gitignore: no built library under tests/ is added again
  * protocol-gen: one helper reads the items of any domain through the
    loader; sabotage arms follow
  * machine domain: the document as it left omx-contract, less the copied
    descriptions
  * machine words: contract.d/machine is plugin-hostd's domain, installed by
    the installer's domain mode (green)
  * tests: the machine words are plugin-hostd's own domain,
    contract.d/machine (red)
  * qualification words: the probe and the schema generator read
    plugin-qualify's domain through the loader, no render here (green)
  * tests: the qualification words are plugin-qualify's domain, read through
    the loader, with no render here (red)
  * sabotage: the pool's table name is a module function, not a lambda
  * sabotage: an arm whose command fails is a named FAIL, not a traceback
  * deps.txt: align the omx-clap-host row with the others
  * tests: the no-pins sabotage arms plant into the lines as the floor re-cut
    renders them
  * deps: floors only, declared once in packaging/deps.txt (re-cut of #132 on
    main)
  * Make the chain-refusal arm tell a refusal from a death again
  * describe fixture: the contract directory's MANIFEST names the digest of
    role-meanings.json as it now reads (red: the describe test refused the
    file as not matching its manifest)
  * schema addresses: the descriptor writer, its fixtures and the
    probe-output schema name https://openmixer.org/schema/, not a
    code-hosting address
  * perturbation: exempt the quiet-exit grace that shares the suspect
    window's value
  * Render the vocabulary with omx-contract 3.19.1
  * Stop a worker without waiting for it to leave
  * Test that stopping a worker that ignores SIGTERM does not hold the daemon
    up
  * Skip the suspect and blame logic for a worker the daemon stopped itself
  * Test that a worker the daemon stops itself blames and drops nothing
  * Ask a worker to leave before killing it, so it closes its JACK client
  * tests: a worker the daemon gives up on is asked to leave before it is
    killed
  * doc_shrink: a remote base is fetched first, and a failed fetch is
    refused, by name
  * tests: a remote doc-gate base is fetched, and a failed fetch is red, by
    name (red)
  * doc_shrink: an empty DOC_GATE_BASE is refused, by name
  * tests: an empty doc-gate base is red, by name (red)
  * doxygen gate: it refuses a header without @file, a missing log, an unread
    header and another doxygen
  * tests: the doxygen gate proves doxygen read every header (red)
  * docs(transforms.h): document the public API (baseline 119 -> 99)
  * docs(history.h): document the public API (baseline 153 -> 119)
  * docs(planner.h): document the public API (baseline 185 -> 153)
  * docs(headers): the documented headers follow the review's style rules
    (baseline 185 -> 185)
  * grouping-reasons: the generator writes the docstring ruff's D rules want
  * docs(writer.h): document the public API (baseline 200 -> 185)
  * docs(json.h): document the public API (baseline 221 -> 200)
  * docs(formats.h): document the public API (baseline 266 -> 221)
  * docs(confine.h): document the public API (baseline 266 -> 266)
  * docs(relay.h): document the public API (baseline 266 -> 266)
  * docs(verbs.h): document the public API (baseline 266 -> 266)
  * docs(session.h): document the public API (baseline 266 -> 266)
  * docs(proc.h): document the public API (baseline 319 -> 291 -> 291)
  * docs(supervisor.h): document the public API (baseline 445 -> 319)
  * tests: the real-doxygen arm reads its header under the repository's
    Doxyfile
  * doxygen gate: doxygen writes throwaway HTML, so it reads @param and
    @return
  * tests: a fully documented function gives no doxygen warning (red)
  * ci: the doc-gates job installs doxygen through tools/bounded-install.sh
  * doc gates: the baseline and the noqa comments only shrink; --update only
    lowers
  * tests: the documentation gates only shrink, by mechanism (red)
  * tests: the build and run arms pass the pkg-config step whatever is
    installed
  * tests: an arm for every test-consumer step, run under $(MAKE)
  * test-consumer names its failing step and pkg-config's reason
  * tests: test-consumer must name its failing step and pkg-config's reason
    (red)
  * tests: the listing shim copies an entry's d_reclen bytes, not a whole
    dirent
  * tests: the bundle rule's listing is the reverse of byte order, so its arm
    can fail
  * tests: the bundle rule's one-directory arm reads a listing the test sets
    (red)
  * Documentation gates by the standard tools: doxygen for C, ruff for Python
  * tests: the dead sabotage-shard machinery goes, the package jobs run a
    named smoke (test audit rows 1, 2, 11)
  * Documentation gates: a C header comment ratchet and ruff D1 on the Python
    clients

